+## C05 libraries and registration
+
+`crown_selection` contains five pure units and links `crown_ranking` plus its
+existing plan/SQL/core chain. It retains typed minimum-height proof authority,
+complete baseline assessments and immutable plan artifacts. Link
+`crown_selection_runtime` explicitly for actual-owner Physical/Delta/Session
+selection. Its one unit links the pure selector and production ranking bridge.
+`crown_selection_runtime_testing` compiles that same unit against only the
+matching testing ranking/runtime bridge. The macro is inherited through that
+target; production and testing runtime variants must not be combined.
+
+The runtime source list remains 14 units, and each report library remains six
+units. Neither depends on selection, and no selection target links a report
+library. The pure link and independent diagnostic-byte tests link without any
+runtime archive. See the [selection guide](selection.md),
+[cache-binding contract](selection_binding.md) and
+[logical accounting contract](selection_accounting.md).
+
+The proposed registration keeps the complete 143-test prefix with identical
+commands, ordering and settings, then appends 15 `C05` tests: ten producer and
+five independent consumers. They cover constrained/unconstrained decisions,
+literal depth and slot values, full source and byte binding, current/as-of
+lifecycle, whole-artifact cache behavior, aggregate budget boundaries and
+persistent allocation failures. The three fault consumers have a 7200-second
+timeout; the other new cases have 900 seconds. All inherit the shared native
+ASan/UBSan environment. The production/testing example objects compile the same
+`tests/examples/selection_usage.cpp` without adding duplicate runtime tests.
+
+The expected compile inventory is 214 existing target/source entries plus five
+pure units, two bridge variants, fifteen consumer units and two example objects:
+238 entries. These counts are registration expectations until root verifies
+actual CMake output. The complete native compiler/sanitizer/clean-source matrix
+is pending; an excluded test result or C05-only subset does not accept it.
+Use `ctest --test-dir build/debug -L C05 --output-on-failure` to select the new
+tests after native integration.
+
+All registered files use native source/include/fixture paths. The C05 tests
+reuse existing checked-in Boolean candidate fixtures; no temporary author
+artifact or excluded verification package is a build/runtime dependency.
+Existing CLI commands and report schemas are unchanged. Selection has no CLI,
+automatic reoptimization, deployment/migration, C03 model or allocator-byte
+prediction. A tuple/index-slot cap is never treated as a memory-byte cap.
